const data = {
  reader: "reader-a",
  inputs_read: [
    "docs/quality/summary-qa/root/2026-11-05-batch-002957/current-snapshot-revalidation-2026-11-07/iteration-02/summary-snapshot.md (complete, lines 1-279)",
    "docs/quality/summary-qa/root/2026-11-05-batch-002957/current-snapshot-revalidation-2026-11-07/iteration-02/questions.json (complete, lines 1-293)"
  ],
  answers: [
    {
      id: "Q01",
      source_passages: [{section:"Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle; Rule (2.5)", quotation:"**Rule (2.5):** A player rules a clearing with more total **warriors plus buildings** than each other player. Tokens and pawns do not contribute. Ordinary ties mean nobody rules. Eyrie rule a tie for most if they have at least one Eyrie piece there. Vagabond cannot rule or stop someone else ruling."}],
      answer: [{part:"Rule determination",ruling:"Compare each player's total warriors plus buildings in the clearing. Tokens and pawns do not count. The player with strictly more than every other player rules; an ordinary tie means nobody rules. The Eyrie rules a tie for the most when it has at least one Eyrie piece there. The Vagabond cannot rule and cannot prevent another player from ruling.",evidence:"Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle; Rule (2.5)"}],
      support:"supported",
      evidence:["Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle; Rule (2.5)"]
    },
    {
      id:"Q02",
      source_passages:[{section:"Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle; Move (4.2)",quotation:"**Move (4.2):** Take any positive number of your warriors/pawns from one clearing along a linking path to an adjacent clearing. You must rule origin or destination or both. Recheck rule for each move. You may move the same pieces repeatedly, including on multiple moves in one action. Rivers are not paths unless an effect explicitly treats them as paths. Moving and placing are different procedures. Vagabond has its own movement exceptions below."}],
      answer:[{part:"Normal move legality",ruling:"A normal move transfers a positive number of your warriors or pawns from one clearing along a linking path to an adjacent clearing, and you must rule at least one endpoint. Recheck rule for every move. The same pieces may move repeatedly, including multiple moves in one action. Rivers are not paths unless an effect explicitly makes them paths. Vagabond-specific movement exceptions are separate.",evidence:"Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle; Move (4.2)"}],
      support:"supported",
      evidence:["Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle; Move (4.2)"]
    },
    {
      id:"Q03",
      source_passages:[{section:"Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle; Battle (4.3)",quotation:"**Battle (4.3):** Choose a clearing with your warriors or pawn and an enemy there as defender. **Battle does not require you to rule the clearing.** Resolve these six steps:\n\n1. **Ambush:** Defender may play one ambush matching clearing (birds are wild). Attacker may foil it with a matching ambush. Defender's card is discarded; a foiled ambush deals no hits. Otherwise defender immediately deals two hits, then discards ambush. If no attacking warriors or pawns remain, battle ends immediately. Ambush hits are not limited by defending warriors.\n2. **Before-roll effects:** Resolve applicable effects; attacker chooses order if both have them.\n3. **Roll:** Higher die is attacker's rolled hits, lower defender's; equal dice give equal results. Each side's rolled hits are capped by its own warriors in battle. Alliance defending reverses the dice; Vagabond uses undamaged swords instead of warriors.\n4. **After-roll effects:** Resolve effects affecting battle that do not say “before rolling”; attacker chooses order if both have them.\n5. **Count hits:** Add extra hits (uncapped by warriors), subtract ignored hits. If defender has no warriors, attacker deals one extra hit for **defenseless**; Vagabond is instead defenseless if it has no undamaged swords.\n6. **Deal hits:** Each hit removes one opposing piece. The side taking hits chooses its own removal order, but **all its warriors must be removed before its buildings/tokens**. It also chooses order of effects triggered by its pieces' removal. Both sides deal their counted hits; losing warriors does not retroactively change the rolled cap. Whoever removes an enemy building/token scores **one VP each**, even while defending and even outside battle. Vagabond takes hits as item damage instead."}],
      answer:[{part:"Battle through removal",ruling:"To initiate, choose a clearing containing your warrior(s) or pawn and an enemy defender; you need not rule it. The defender may ambush with a matching card (bird wild). The attacker may foil with a matching ambush; then the defender's card is discarded and it deals no hits. Otherwise the ambush deals two immediate hits, regardless of defending warrior count, and is discarded. If no attacking warriors or pawns remain, battle ends immediately. Resolve applicable before-roll effects (attacker orders them when both sides have effects), roll with higher die as attacker hits and lower as defender hits (ties give equal results), and cap each side's rolled hits at its own warriors in battle. Alliance defending reverses the dice; Vagabond uses undamaged swords instead of warriors. Resolve applicable after-roll effects, with attacker choosing order where both sides have them. Count hits by adding extra hits without a warrior cap and subtracting ignored hits; a defender without warriors gives attacker one defenseless hit, while Vagabond is defenseless only with no undamaged swords. For each hit remove one opposing piece. The side taking hits chooses its own removal order, but must remove all warriors before buildings/tokens, and chooses the order of its piece-removal effects. Both sides deal counted hits; later warrior losses do not change the rolled cap. Each enemy building or token removed scores one VP for whoever removes it, even while defending and outside battle. Vagabond takes hits as item damage.",evidence:"Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle; Battle (4.3)"}],
      support:"supported",
      evidence:["Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle; Battle (4.3)"]
    },
    {
      id:"Q04",
      source_passages:[
        {section:"Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle; Craft (4.1) and Personal duplicate check",quotation:"**Craft (4.1):** **Every crafting piece gets its suit from the clearing containing it.** The card's **bottom-left crafting icons** require pieces of those clearing suits; the card's own suit does not define the cost. Craft a card from hand when your faction permits.\n\n**Personal duplicate check:** Only an identical persistent effect **in your own play area** prevents you from crafting that effect again. Other players' copies do not count for this duplicate restriction."},
        {section:"Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle; Marquise, Eyrie and Alliance cost; Vagabond cost and reuse; three-color icon",quotation:"- **Marquise, Eyrie and Alliance cost:** For **each icon**, activate **one workshop, roost or sympathy in a clearing matching that icon's suit**, respectively. A crafting piece gets its suit from its clearing. Combine eligible pieces as needed, but **each piece may activate only once per turn**.\n- **Vagabond cost and reuse:** The pawn **may activate repeatedly in a turn**. For each icon, **pay by exhausting one face-up, undamaged hammer: flip that hammer face down**. The pawn's **current clearing must match every icon on the card**. Reusing the pawn never waives the hammer payment per icon. One clearing cannot pay mixed fox/rabbit/mouse icons.\n- A **three-color question-mark icon** accepts any suit."},
        {section:"Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle; Craft immediate effect",quotation:"- Immediate effect (paper box): resolve, then discard the **crafting card**. An item card requires the corresponding **item token** in the map supply, or it cannot be crafted. Take the item token into Crafted Items and score the VP printed on the card, subject to Eyrie exception. The item token stays; the crafting card is discarded. Ordinary factions do not exhaust crafted items as Vagabond does."}
      ],
      answer:[
        {part:"Cost and suit",ruling:"Read the bottom-left crafting icons; each crafting piece gets its suit from its clearing, not from the card. Marquise, Eyrie and Alliance pay one matching workshop, roost or sympathy per icon, respectively; pieces can be combined but each activates only once per turn. Vagabond can reuse its pawn, but pays one face-up undamaged hammer per icon and its current clearing must match every icon; one clearing cannot satisfy mixed suits. A three-color question-mark icon accepts any suit.",evidence:"Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle; Craft (4.1), faction crafting costs"},
        {part:"Item supply and duplicate persistent effect",ruling:"An item card cannot be crafted if its corresponding item token is absent from the map supply. Only an identical persistent effect already in your own play area prevents crafting that effect again; another player's copy does not. The cited immediate-effect rule also says the item token goes into Crafted Items and the crafting card is discarded after resolving.",evidence:"Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle; Personal duplicate check, immediate effect"}
      ],
      support:"supported",
      evidence:["Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle; Craft (4.1), Personal duplicate check, faction crafting costs, immediate effect"]
    },
    {
      id:"Q05",
      source_passages:[{section:"Scoring / Victory Conditions; Dominance (3.3)",quotation:"**Dominance (3.3):** In own Daylight at **at least 10 VP**, activate a dominance card from hand into play area; remove score marker and stop scoring VP. Cannot remove/replace activated card. At **start of own Birdsong**, win if ruling **three clearings of matching mouse/rabbit/fox suit**, or for **bird dominance, two diagonally opposite corner clearings**. Meeting condition earlier does not immediately win. Dominance cards cannot be crafted, but can be spent for suit. Whenever one would enter discard, put it near map available instead. During own Daylight, spend matching card to take available dominance into hand. Available **bird dominance remains bird**, so payment must be bird; a bird hand card can pay for non-bird dominance. Activation and taking are separate, neither requires a faction action allowance."}],
      answer:[{part:"Activation and win conditions",ruling:"Activate a dominance card from hand into the play area during your own Daylight at 10 or more VP; remove your score marker and stop scoring VP. At the start of your own Birdsong, win by ruling three clearings matching the mouse, rabbit or fox suit shown by dominance, or, for bird dominance, by ruling two diagonally opposite corner clearings. Fulfilling a condition earlier does not win immediately. Once activated, the card cannot be removed or replaced.",evidence:"Scoring / Victory Conditions; Dominance (3.3)"}],
      support:"supported",
      evidence:["Scoring / Victory Conditions; Dominance (3.3)"]
    }
  ]
};
