{"section":"Setup; Standard Setup (Law 5.1)","quotation":"Use **Standard Setup**, in this order (Law 5.1):\n\n1. Choose factions; determine starting player and seating randomly. Take faction boards and their listed pieces. Use Fall or Winter. Fall has no special rules; on Winter, the river divides forests just as printed paths do. Rivers are otherwise not paths.\n2. Put score markers at 0.\n3. With two players, remove all four dominance cards. Shuffle shared deck; each player draws **three cards**.\n4. **Ruins and items:** Cover the four R building slots with ruins. The separate map item supply is **2 boots, 2 bags, 1 crossbow, 1 hammer, 2 swords, 2 tea, 2 coins**. Keep the four R-marked ruin items separate from this supply: only Vagabond faction setup hides one each of its R-marked bag, boot, hammer and sword beneath the four ruins, **one item beneath each ruin**. During that Vagabond setup, shuffle the ruin/item stacks and return each to an empty R ruin slot, keeping item identities hidden. Without a Vagabond, ruins contain no items.\n5. The map item supply uses its corresponding spaces near the top of the map.\n6. Distribute overview cards as desired; put battle dice nearby.\n7. Set up factions in their letter order: Marquise, Eyrie, Alliance, Vagabond. Setup order is distinct from turn order."},
{"section":"Setup; Hidden ruin items (only when Vagabond is present, during its faction setup)","quotation":"**Hidden ruin items (only when Vagabond is present, during its faction setup):**\n\n1. Take the four ruins and R-marked bag, boot, hammer and sword. Put **one item beneath each ruin**.\n2. **Shuffle the ruin/item stacks**, keeping identities hidden.\n3. **Return each stack to an empty R ruin slot** on the map. With no Vagabond, leave the four ruins without hidden items."}
],
"answer":[
