"source_passages":[{"section":"Eyrie Dynasties (7); Daylight — resolve the Decree","quotation":"**Daylight — resolve the Decree:** Craft using roosts first, then resolve **every Decree card**, column by column **Recruit → Move → Battle → Build**. Within one column choose card order freely. Bird is wild. **If any required action cannot be fully completed, immediately enter Turmoil: you cannot skip the card or continue other columns.** For a prompted placement with too few pieces, first place the maximum possible, then enter Turmoil because the action remains incomplete (publisher clarification in **FAQ & Rulings**). Each card requires:\n\n| Decree column | Match the card's suit to | Required procedure for one card |\n|---|---|---|\n| Recruit | Clearing with a roost | Place **one warrior at one chosen roost** there; Charismatic must instead place **two warriors** there |\n| Move | Origin clearing | Move **at least one warrior**, obeying ordinary path and rule requirements |\n| Battle | Clearing of battle | Initiate a battle there with Eyrie warriors and an enemy |\n| Build | Target clearing | Place one roost in a clearing you rule, with an open slot and **no roost already there** |\n\n**Bird Decree cards are wild in every column:** choose any clearing suit, while still meeting that action’s other requirements.\n\nIf a prompted placement runs short, place the maximum possible first, as clarified in **FAQ & Rulings**. If the required action cannot be completed fully for any reason (including warrior/building supply), immediately enter **Turmoil**; do not skip that card or continue other Decree columns. With Charismatic and only one warrior available, place that one, then enter Turmoil: one does not fulfill the required two."}],
"answer":[
{"part":"Sequence and card suits","ruling":"First craft using roosts. Then resolve every Decree card column by column in Recruit, Move, Battle, Build order; within a column, choose the card order freely. The card's suit matches the relevant location: a clearing with a roost for Recruit, the origin for Move, the battle clearing for Battle, and the target clearing for Build. Bird cards are wild in all columns, but still must meet the action's other requirements.","evidence":"Eyrie Dynasties (7); Daylight — resolve the Decree"},
{"part":"Required action per card","ruling":"Recruit places one warrior at one chosen roost, or two there under Charismatic. Move at least one warrior while obeying ordinary path and rule requirements. Battle initiates a battle in the matching clearing with Eyrie warriors and an enemy. Build places one roost in a clearing the Eyrie rules, with an open slot and no roost already there.","evidence":"Eyrie Dynasties (7); Daylight — resolve the Decree"},
{"part":"Incomplete action","ruling":"Every Decree card is compulsory. If any required action cannot be fully completed, immediately enter Turmoil; do not skip that card or continue to another column. If a prompted placement is short, place the maximum possible first, then enter Turmoil because the action is still incomplete. This also applies to supply shortages: with Charismatic and only one warrior, place that one and then enter Turmoil; it does not fulfill the requirement for two.","evidence":"Eyrie Dynasties (7); Daylight — resolve the Decree"}
